WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:17.593
Mowgli could smell things better than most humans could.

2
00:00:17.594 --> 00:00:20.726
But he did not have a true jungle nose.

3
00:00:20.727 --> 00:00:26.892
So it took him longer to find the scent.

4
00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.970
"It's Buldeo!" he whispered.

5
00:00:29.971 --> 00:00:32.593
"He must have followed my trail.

6
00:00:32.594 --> 00:00:37.314
I can see the sunlight glinting off his gun. Look!"

7
00:00:37.315 --> 00:00:40.975
There was just a quick flash of light among some shrubs.

8
00:00:40.976 --> 00:00:43.167
But they all saw it.

9
00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:47.394
The four young wolves suddenly ran downhill.

10
00:00:47.395 --> 00:00:51.124
"Where are you going?" Mowgli said.

11
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:53.936
"Hunting!" Gray Brother answered.

12
00:00:53.937 --> 00:00:56.288
"Come on with us!"

13
00:00:56.289 --> 00:01:00.658
"I can't. Humans do not hunt other humans!"

14
00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:03.003
Mowgli called after them.

15
00:01:03.004 --> 00:01:07.189
Akela gazed at him, and Mowgli looked away.

16
00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:13.239
"Let's just find this man and see what he wants," Bagheera said.

17
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:20.751
Mowgli ran forward, darting noiselessly through the jungle behind the young wolves.

18
00:01:20.752 --> 00:01:25.266
The others followed.

19
00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:31.416
Sure enough, when Mowgli pushed aside some bushes, there was Buldeo.

20
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:36.034
His gun on one shoulder, the hunter trotted along the path.

21
00:01:36.035 --> 00:01:40.824
Abruptly he halted, looking at the ground in confusion.

22
00:01:40.825 --> 00:01:45.473
Akela chuckled softly from beside Mowgli.

23
00:01:45.474 --> 00:01:48.969
"This morning I added some prints to the trail.

24
00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:52.589
They're going in all different directions."

25
00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:58.561
"No wonder Buldeo is confused," Mowgli whispered with a grin.

26
00:01:58.562 --> 00:02:02.437
Finally the hunter grunted and sat down.

27
00:02:02.438 --> 00:02:08.417
He had no idea that Mowgli and the animals were nearby, watching him.

28
00:02:08.418 --> 00:02:11.758
He muttered angrily to himself.

29
00:02:11.759 --> 00:02:15.769
"What is he saying?" Bagheera asked Mowgli.

30
00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:19.055
He quickly translated Buldeo's words.

31
00:02:19.056 --> 00:02:23.574
"He says, 'packs of wolves must have danced round me.

32
00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:27.337
I never saw a trail like this!'

33
00:02:27.338 --> 00:02:31.649
Now he's complaining about being tired and hungry."

34
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.959
Buldeo ate some nuts.

35
00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.825
Soon some other men wandered along the trail.

36
00:02:38.826 --> 00:02:41.798
They sat down for a rest too.

37
00:02:41.799 --> 00:02:46.660
Buldeo began telling them some wild stories.

38
00:02:46.661 --> 00:02:50.319
Mowgli nearly laughed aloud as he listened.

39
00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.270
Buldeo was telling the men that he had killed the great tiger, Shere Khan.

40
00:02:55.271 --> 00:02:59.950
Then he said that a boy had turned himself into a wolf.

41
00:02:59.951 --> 00:03:04.246
"I fought with him all afternoon," the hunter said.

42
00:03:04.247 --> 00:03:08.378
"I think he used magic on my gun."

43
00:03:08.379 --> 00:03:12.355
"What makes you say that?" one of the men asked.

44
00:03:12.356 --> 00:03:16.629
"A bullet meant for him suddenly spun around.

45
00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.834
It went into one of my own buffalo!

46
00:03:19.835 --> 00:03:21.509
I'm the chief hunter.

47
00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:25.237
So my village has sent me to hunt him down."

48
00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:28.520
Mowgli's friends glanced over, worried.

49
00:03:28.521 --> 00:03:31.753
However, Mowgli was still grinning.

50
00:03:31.754 --> 00:03:34.505
"His stories are ridiculous.

51
00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:37.806
But the other men believe him!"

52
00:03:37.807 --> 00:03:43.832
"Meanwhile the villagers have locked up Messua and her husband," Buldeo was saying.

53
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:46.260
"They are sorcerers too.

54
00:03:46.261 --> 00:03:51.778
In fact, they are the worst kind because they were raising this wolf child.

55
00:03:51.779 --> 00:03:56.576
They will be punished—perhaps even burned to death."

56
00:03:56.577 --> 00:04:02.056
The men gasped. "When?" one asked.

57
00:04:02.057 --> 00:04:08.613
"Nothing will be done until I return with the boy's dead body," Buldeo replied.

58
00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:14.553
"By the way, I have reason to think he's nearby. Have you seen him?"

59
00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:17.615
Bagheera glanced at Mowgli again.

60
00:04:17.616 --> 00:04:21.742
He noticed that the boy's expression had changed.

61
00:04:21.743 --> 00:04:25.410
"What are the men saying?" the panther whispered.

62
00:04:25.411 --> 00:04:29.436
With a grim look, Mowgli translated.

63
00:04:29.437 --> 00:04:34.445
He explained the villagers had trapped Messua and her husband.

64
00:04:34.446 --> 00:04:39.518
"What?" Gray Brother shook his head in confusion.

65
00:04:39.519 --> 00:04:43.214
"Humans trap each other?"

66
00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:47.559
"So Buldeo says." Mowgli scowled.

67
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:53.191
"I cannot understand all his talk—people are crazy.

68
00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:59.269
But I do know this: Messua and her husband have done nothing wrong.

69
00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:03.289
All they did was feed me and shelter me."

70
00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.657
Mowgli listened to Buldeo some more.

71
00:05:06.658 --> 00:05:10.417
His expression grew more and more determined.

72
00:05:10.418 --> 00:05:13.351
"I am going back to the village.

73
00:05:13.352 --> 00:05:18.307
I won't let them kill Messua!"
